{"created": "2022-11-21T17:07:30.680161+00:00", "modified": "2026-04-22T23:24:42.644454+00:00", "id": 7342768, "conceptrecid": "7342767", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7342768", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.7342767", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7342768", "metadata": {"title": "Colgen -  Collective Genealogies Visualisation and Analysis", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.7342768", "publication_date": "2019-12-02", "description": "<p>Colgen is a python package to visualise and analyse collective-level genealogies. Its features include:</p>\n\n<p>- Visualise propagation-replacement data in the form of a tree where each node correspond to a collective, interactively (served locally as HTML) or statically (using the python API).</p>\n\n<p>- Build a Binary Bayesian Network representation of the genealogy where each node display (1) or not (0) a mutation. Use a Maximum-a-posteriori method to infer probable the location of mutations in the genealogy (from a few sequenced points).</p>\n\n<p>- Build a Continuous Bayesian Network representation of the genealogy where each node is associated with a survival probability. Use a Maximum-a-posteriori method to infer locations in the genealogy where this probability changes. &nbsp;</p>\n\n<p>For more information see the readme file. Development is ongoing.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Guilhem Doulcier", "affiliation": "Universit\u00e9 Paris Sciences et Lettres", "orcid": "0000-0003-3720-9089"}], "keywords": ["Bayesian network", "Visualisation", "Experimental evolution"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://gitlab.com/ecoevomath/colgen/-/tree/master/colgen", "relation": "isPublishedIn", "resource_type": "software", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "https://pastel.archives-ouvertes.fr/tel-02917058", "relation": "isDescribedBy", "resource_type": "publication-dissertation", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "grants": [{"c